{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.Model.GLnRMatrix","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.Model.GLnRMatrix","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Monoidal.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Basis","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.StdBasis","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Module","lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.HeckeCrossing"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S_ne_smul_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S_ne_smul_id","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L211-L226","doc":"**Nondegeneracy of the crossing.**  For `n ≥ 2` (and `R` nontrivial) the crossing is not a\nscalar multiple of the identity: `Ř (e_0 ⊗ e_1)` has a nonzero `e_1 ⊗ e_0` component.  So the\n`H_m(q)`-action on `X^{⊗ m}` does not factor through the trivial character, unlike the\none-dimensional `unitDatum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.crossing_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.crossing_S","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L209-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.crossing","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L203-L207","doc":"**The `GL_n` R-matrix is a Hecke crossing** on `X = R^n`, for every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.braid","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L182-L201","doc":"**Relation (2): the braid (Yang–Baxter) relation** for `Ř` on `X ⊗ (X ⊗ X)`, for every `n`.\nThe proof evaluates both sides on `e_a ⊗ (e_b ⊗ e_c)` and splits on the relative order of\n`a, b, c`; only the two cases `a = b < c` and `a < b = c` use `q * qi = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.quad","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L166-L179","doc":"**Relation (1): the Hecke quadratic relation** `Ř² = (q - qi) Ř + (q qi) 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.tacticFin_omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.tacticFin_omega","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L163-L164","doc":"Decide an order (in)equality between elements of `Fin n` from the hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S_whiskerLeft_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S_whiskerLeft_apply","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L159-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S_whiskerRight_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S_whiskerRight_apply","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L156-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.hom_assoc_inv_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.hom_assoc_inv_apply","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L151-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.hom_assoc_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.hom_assoc_apply","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L149-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.hom_ext3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.hom_ext3","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L133-L143","doc":"Two morphisms out of `X ⊗ (X ⊗ X)` agree if they agree on the basis `e_a ⊗ (e_b ⊗ e_c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.bas3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.bas3","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L129-L131","doc":"The basis `e_a ⊗ (e_b ⊗ e_c)` of `X ⊗ (X ⊗ X)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.hom_ext2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.hom_ext2","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L119-L126","doc":"Two morphisms out of `X ⊗ X` agree if they agree on the basis `e_i ⊗ e_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S_ee","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S_ee","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L116-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.S","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L113-L114","doc":"`Ř` as a morphism `X ⊗ X ⟶ X ⊗ X` of `ModuleCat R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.rLin_ee","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.rLin_ee","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L109-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.rLin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.rLin","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L106-L107","doc":"`Ř` as a linear endomorphism of the raw tensor square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.bas_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.bas_apply","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnRMatrix.lean#L103-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.bas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.bas","kind":"def",